{# The shares are printed rather than written out, from the same numbers the
   prices are worked out with -- Party::shares(). They are the figures most
   likely to be tuned, and a page quoting them from memory would be the last
   place anybody looked. The two tax lines are words because they are
   structural: a child holds a seat and is taxed like an adult, a lap infant
   holds none and is not taxed at all. #}
{% set shares = party_shares() %}

<h2>Three kinds of traveller</h2>
<p>
    An adult is 12 or over. A child is 2 to 11 and gets a seat. A lap infant is
    under 2 and travels on an adult&rsquo;s lap with no seat of their own.
</p>
<p>
    Which one a child counts as decides both what they pay and how many of you
    can travel on one booking.
</p>

<h2>What each one pays</h2>
<p>Fares here are quoted per adult, and everyone else is a share of that:</p>
<ul>
    <li>
        A child pays <strong>{{ (shares.child_fare * 100)|round }}%</strong> of
        the adult fare and the tax in full. A seat is a seat.
    </li>
    <li>
        A lap infant pays <strong>{{ (shares.infant_fare * 100)|round }}%</strong>
        of the adult fare and no tax at all.
    </li>
</ul>
<p>This is why a party of four does not cost four times a party of one.</p>

<h2>What the search will not accept</h2>
<ul>
    <li>At least one adult. Somebody has to be responsible for the booking.</li>
    <li>No more infants than adults. A lap needs an adult attached to it.</li>
    <li>
        {{ max_seats }} seats at most. Infants are not counted against it,
        because they are not in one.
    </li>
</ul>

<h2>At checkout, and on the day</h2>
<p>
    Each child needs a date of birth that matches the type they were booked as.
    A date that disagrees is refused &mdash; see
    <a href="/help/passenger-details">changing passenger details</a>.
</p>
<p>
    Everything about the flight itself belongs to the airline: bassinets,
    strollers, and whether a child may fly unaccompanied at all. Its page here
    has its phone number &mdash; see <a href="/airlines">all airlines</a>.
</p>
